- Or Disciple (1/3) for 1 black\n\
- Or Wakedancer (??/???) for 2 black\n\
\n\
The Bone Picker is a FLYING creature with DEATHTOUCH - that's powerful! But wait, let me check Bone Picker's oracle text again - \"This spell costs {3} less to cast if a creature died this turn\". \n\
\n\
Has a creature died THIS turn? No! The last death was my Soulcage Fiend on the opponent's turn 5. So the discount doesn't apply anymore!\n\
\n\
That means Bone Picker costs full {3}{B} = 4 mana. I have 4 black mana. I can afford it!\n\
\n\
But let me also check Wakedancer's cost. I should cast the Wakedancer first to understand its value, then decide on sequencing.\n\
\n\
Actually, looking at the choices, I can play multiple creatures. Let me cast the Disciple first (1B), which leaves me 3 black. Then I can cast Wakedancer (2B), leaving 1 black. Then I can't afford Bone Picker (needs 4).\n\
\n\
