      "reasoning": "I can block with Wakedancer (2/2 vs Preston 2/5)! Wakedancer will die. But Wakedancer is currently sick, so... wait, let me check. The status says \"sick\" which usually means summoning sickness. But can I still declare it as a blocker? Typically, summoning sickness only prevents attacking, not blocking!\n\
\n\
So I CAN block with Wakedancer! The Wakedancer will die (taking 2 damage from Preston while dealing 2 back), and my life will stay the same (instead of taking 2 damage).\n\
\n\
But should I block? Let me think:\n\
- If I block: Wakedancer dies (trades 2 for 2), but I lose a creature\n\
- If I don't block: I take 2 damage (15 -> 13), but Wakedancer stays alive\n\
\n\
Actually, blocking is GOOD! Preston is 2/5, Wakedancer is 2/2. Preston will still survive (2/3 remaining), but I trade my Wakedancer for damage prevention. But since I'm already at 15 life and the opponent is at 15, staying even on life total while removing my blockers is NOT ideal!\n\
\n\
Let me NOT block and take the 2 damage!",
