      "description": "GPT54 Sport passed priority in precombat main with 6 untapped lands and three castable spells, effectively ending their turn without doing anything. They have Blessed Sanctuary and Preston on board, making creature spells especially valuable. Faith's Fetters could lock down a threat and gain 4 life. Brightmare could tap a creature, gain life, and create a 2/2 Unicorn via Blessed Sanctuary. This wastes an entire turn of development.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without casting any spell, effectively ending the turn.",
      "better_line": "Cast Faith's Fetters on Durable Coilbug or Wakedancer to neutralize a threat and gain 4 life, then cast Brightmare with remaining mana to tap another creature, gain life, and create a 2/2 Unicorn token from Blessed Sanctuary. At minimum, cast at least one of the three available spells.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 157,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 130,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Blocked Durable Coilbug with the Unicorn Token instead of Wakedancer. Durable Coilbug has a {4}{B} recursion ability from the graveyard, so killing it in combat is less permanent than killing Wakedancer. Either way 2 damage gets through unblocked, but trading the token into Wakedancer would permanently remove a threat rather than one that can be rebought.",
      "action_taken": "Unicorn Token blocks Durable Coilbug (which has graveyard recursion)",
      "better_line": "Unicorn Token blocks Wakedancer (permanently removing it), let Durable Coilbug through for the same 2 damage",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 197,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 163,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Passed priority in precombat main phase with 7 untapped lands and multiple powerful plays available. Emiel the Blessed (4 mana) creates a devastating engine with the existing Preston + Blessed Sanctuary board, and Faith's Fetters could neutralize the opponent's Bone Picker (3/2 flying deathtouch). The player essentially skipped their entire turn for no reason.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority with 7 untapped mana, ending the main phase without casting anything.",
      "better_line": "Cast Emiel the Blessed for 4 mana, creating a powerful flicker engine with Preston and Blessed Sanctuary already on board. This would also trigger Blessed Sanctuary to create a 2/2 Unicorn token. Could potentially also cast Faith's Fetters on Bone Picker with remaining 3 mana (needs 4, so would need to sequence differently - cast Fetters first or just Emiel). At minimum, Emiel is an incredible play here.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 206,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 170,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "With Emiel the Blessed on the battlefield, 3 untapped Plains, Preston the Vanisher, Blessed Sanctuary, and Brightmare all in play, GPT54 Sport declined to pay {3} to flicker Brightmare. Flickering Brightmare would have triggered Preston (creating a 0/1 Illusion copy of Brightmare), Blessed Sanctuary (creating a 2/2 Unicorn), and two Brightmare ETBs (tapping two enemy creatures and gaining life). This is a huge value play that was missed.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Emiel's flicker ability, wasting 3 available mana.",
      "better_line": "Activate Emiel the Blessed targeting Brightmare for {3}, generating multiple tokens and ETB triggers with Preston and Blessed Sanctuary on the battlefield, while tapping down opponent's threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 224,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 183,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "With 3 untapped Plains and Emiel the Blessed's activated ability available, GPT54 Sport could flicker Brightmare to trigger a powerful chain: Brightmare ETB (tap a creature + gain life), Blessed Sanctuary (create 2/2 Unicorn), Preston (create Illusion copy of Brightmare which itself triggers another tap + life gain + another Unicorn). This would generate 2+ extra tokens, tap down opponent's threats, and gain significant life, all while the opponent is at just 7 life. Instead, the mana went unused.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without activating Emiel the Blessed, wasting 3 available mana.",
      "better_line": "Activate Emiel the Blessed targeting Brightmare to flicker it, generating multiple ETB triggers through Blessed Sanctuary and Preston, creating additional tokens and tapping opponent's creatures to set up a dominant board position and likely lethal next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 226,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 185,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Declined to pay {G/W} for Emiel the Blessed's trigger on a Unicorn token, missing two free +1/+1 counters. With 3 untapped Plains and no castable spells in hand (Faith's Fetters costs 4, Rambunctious Mutt costs 5), the mana would have gone unused anyway.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to pay {G/W} for Emiel's counter trigger",
      "better_line": "Pay {W} from an untapped Plains to put two +1/+1 counters on the Unicorn token, making it a 4/4 for free",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 228,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 187,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Passed priority in postcombat main phase with an unplayed land drop (Plains in hand) and castable Faith's Fetters (4 mana, 7 untapped lands). Faith's Fetters on Morkrut Banshee 4/4 would neutralize the opponent's biggest threat and gain 4 life, while the missed land drop is pure waste. With the opponent at 7 life and a dominant board, this delays closing out the game.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority, ending the turn without playing the Plains from hand or casting any spells.",
      "better_line": "Play Plains (free land drop), then cast Faith's Fetters targeting Morkrut Banshee 4/4 to lock it down and gain 4 life, setting up a likely lethal attack next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 283,
      "player": "GPT54 Sport",
      "decision_index": 225,
    }
  ],
